  "name": "Trance & Acid",
  "editorial_article": "Released 8 February 2002 via Sony Dance Division, Trance & Acid stands as the second studio album from German producer Kai Tracid. The 13-track collection leans heavily into acid house textures and hard trance rhythms, featuring vocal contributions from Jade 4U on tracks including 'Destiny's Path' and the title song 'Trance & Acid.' The release was distributed in multiple configurations, including a standard CD and a limited edition featuring a bonus DVD with music videos and artist biography. Among the tracklist are four singles: 'Tiefenrausch (The Deep Blue),' 'Too Many Times,' 'Life Is Too Short,' and the eponymous 'Trance & Acid.' Beyond original compositions like 'Bad Shape' and 'Message Without Words,' the album includes a 'Warmduscher Remix' of 'Destiny's Path.'",
